hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"274","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman Al-Muradi told us, Shuaib, meaning Ibn Al-Layth, informed us on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Hormuz, on the authority of Umayr, the client of Ibn Abbas, that he heard him say: I and Abdullah bin Yasar, the client of Maimuna, the husband of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, until we went to Abu Al-Juhaym bin Al-Harith bin Al-Simah Al-Ansari, and Abu Juhaym said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has come. From near a camel's well, a man met him and greeted him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not respond until he approached the wall and wiped his face. And his hands spread it over him.”"
